{"step_index":281,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T12:20:22Z","content":"The test on **`172.30.39.153`** (port `30`, admin user `superuser`) was executed end-to-end and was a complete success.\n\nHere is the full breakdown of what was discovered, configured, and verified:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Pre-Flight & Hardening Discovery\n\nDuring the diagnostic phase on `172.30.39.153`, the script inspected the live OpenSSH daemon configuration and adapted to the server's security policies:\n\n1. **`AllowGroups SSH_Users`**: The target server restricts SSH logins strictly to members of `SSH_Users`. The script added `koby-bowser-ansible` to both `sudo` and `SSH_Users` so OpenSSH wouldn't reject the connection.\n2. **Centralized `AuthorizedKeysFile`**: Instead of the standard `~/.ssh/authorized_keys`, this server specifies `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/%u`. The script detected this dynamically and installed your Debian Trixie Ed25519 public key directly to `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/koby-bowser-ansible` (`chmod 600`), while also populating `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` as fallback.\n3. **Passwordless Sudo**: Configured `/etc/sudoers.d/koby-bowser-ansible` (`0440`).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: First Execution (Bootstrap & Initial Copy)\n\n```bash\n/home/koby/.ansible/scripts/copy-to-remote.sh -p 30 -a superuser 172.30.39.153 /home/koby/ansible-test-payload.txt\n```\n\n**Execution Log Summary:**\n- <span style=\"color:yellow\">**[INFO]**</span> `User 'koby-bowser-ansible' is NOT accessible via passwordless SSH. Initiating bootstrap via administrative account 'superuser'...`\n- Connected via `superuser@172.30.39.153:30`, created account, configured groups and keys.\n- <span style=\"color:green\">**[OK]**</span> `Verified! Passwordless SSH login successful as 'koby-bowser-ansible'.`\n- <span style=\"color:blue\">**Ansible Playbook Run**</span>:\n  ```text\n  PLAY [Validate local source file] **********************************************\n  ok: [lo